{"id": "gsm8k:591", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753284.0688136, "first_event_seconds": 1.052621034963522, "wall_seconds": 53.130102169991005, "prompt_sha256": "b325453bba958b796ceffa32c94af4dc85815ce182e913ceac5ce28581b7416f", "prompt_tokens": 169, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 220, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "f452ce5527c84401ad2daefcd2d54509", "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. The first dog is an Affenpinscher, who weighs 10 pounds.\n2. The second dog is a Dachshund, who weighs twice as much as the Affenpinscher.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight of Dachshund} = 2 \\times 10 = 20 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n3. The third dog is a Papillon, who weighs one-fourth as much as the Dachshund.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight of Papillon} = \\frac{20}{4} = 5 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n4. The fourth dog is a Mastiff, who weighs 44 times as much as the Papillon.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight of Mastiff} = 44 \\times 5 = 220 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the weight of the Mastiff is \\(\\boxed{220}\\) pounds.", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "220", "gsm_numeric_answer": "220", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 220, "entry_transfer_id": "2c811305-2c0d-4924-9601-fd32920bc07a", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.10636340302880853, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
