{"id": "gsm8k:1009", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753592.8252208, "first_event_seconds": 0.9298387030139565, "wall_seconds": 77.29268014000263, "prompt_sha256": "0ecf92ba90162f50147156e22b8d1c79cfdd3d54dc1033f0f1444ab7ec30e00e", "prompt_tokens": 132, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 341, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "98b3aad35e5b4a0995985e544ed7e3d0", "text": "Step 1: Calculate the number of students over 16 years old.\n- Total students: 3000\n- Half of these students are over 16: \\( \\frac{3000}{2} = 1500 \\)\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of male students over 16 years old.\n- One-fourth of the students over 16 are male: \\( \\frac{1500}{4} = 375 \\)\n\nStep 3: Calculate the number of female students over 16 years old.\n- The rest of the students over 16 are female: \\( 1500 - 375 = 1125 \\)\n\nStep 4: Calculate the number of students under 16 years old.\n- The other half of the students are under 16: \\( \\frac{3000}{2} = 1500 \\)\n\nStep 5: Calculate the number of male students under 16 years old.\n- Half of the students under 16 are male: \\( \\frac{1500}{2} = 750 \\)\n\nStep 6: Calculate the number of female students under 16 years old.\n- The rest of the students under 16 are female: \\( 1500 - 750 = 750 \\)\n\nStep 7: Calculate the total number of female students.\n- Total female students: \\( 1125 + 750 = 1875 \\)\n\nFinal: 1875", "final_answer": "1875", "gold_answer": "1,875", "gsm_numeric_answer": "1875", "gsm_extraction": "FINAL", "truncated": false, "events": 341, "entry_transfer_id": "9017c6d1-a0db-45bf-bb6a-850b68ebb573", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.2098267879919149, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
