{"id": "gsm8k:406", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753813.1770897, "first_event_seconds": 1.0992092809756286, "wall_seconds": 47.014191713009495, "prompt_sha256": "006509a4439277205dff6af5d863e65250abcc86daf1b2059b5ca81a451f664e", "prompt_tokens": 122, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 210, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "f0330c7d68e640f2b61558e232e615d6", "text": "Step 1: Determine the initial number of corns.\n- Given that there are twice as many corns as cannolis, and there are 40 cannolis, the number of corns is \\(2 \\times 40 = 80\\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate the new number of cannolis after buying more.\n- Allan bought 60 more cannolis, so the new total number of cannolis is \\(40 + 60 = 100\\).\n\nStep 3: Calculate the new number of corns after buying more.\n- Allan bought 40 fewer corns than the number of cannolis he bought, so the new number of corns is \\(80 - 40 = 40\\).\n\nStep 4: Find the combined total of corns and cannolis.\n- The combined total is \\(100 + 40 = 140\\).\n\nFinal answer:\n\\[\n\\text{FINAL: } 140\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "200", "gsm_numeric_answer": "140", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 210, "entry_transfer_id": "70abe1fb-8127-45bb-a7da-1065d630749a", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.10666190198389813, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
{"id": "gsm8k:1213", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753860.3033743, "first_event_seconds": 0.9361583890276961, "wall_seconds": 47.73170063103316, "prompt_sha256": "8b057aecb28b9f580256a27c44f35a28fa7e9907459fabbc0090d888ed5f1e71", "prompt_tokens": 119, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 213, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "2b74265d8ad54bdab4b5ea005096cec2", "text": "First, let's calculate the total amount Stephen will owe his sister including the 2% interest.\n\n1. **Calculate the interest:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Interest} = 300 \\times 0.02 = 6\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total amount to be returned:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total amount} = 300 + 6 = 306\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total amount Stephen will pay in the first 11 months:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total monthly payments} = 25 \\times 11 = 275\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the remaining amount to be paid in the twelfth month:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining amount} = 306 - 275 = 31\n   \\]\n\nThus, the amount Stephen will pay in the twelfth month is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{31}\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "31", "gsm_numeric_answer": "31", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 213, "entry_transfer_id": "2a5c6016-a12a-4d04-a8e6-a9f69867c3c9", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.3115009720204398, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
{"id": "gsm8k:1289", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753908.354387, "first_event_seconds": 1.121507048024796, "wall_seconds": 67.40049594204174, "prompt_sha256": "8857310c18bf93ab5b5c23f3b2c1f03efcee52625d6436fce7eaf3eb1b790197", "prompt_tokens": 139, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 283, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "cafb39cd54a244a691219b9ecc914606", "text": "To find the total square footage of the quilt, we need to calculate the square footage contributed by each size of t-shirt and then sum these values.\n\n1. **Calculate the square footage from the small t-shirts:**\n   - Each small t-shirt is 3 square feet.\n   - Octavia uses 11 small t-shirts.\n   - Total square footage from small t-shirts: \\( 11 \\times 3 = 33 \\) square feet.\n\n2. **Calculate the square footage from the medium t-shirts:**\n   - Each medium t-shirt is 4 square feet.\n   - Octavia uses 8 medium t-shirts.\n   - Total square footage from medium t-shirts: \\( 8 \\times 4 = 32 \\) square feet.\n\n3. **Calculate the square footage from the large t-shirts:**\n   - Each large t-shirt is 6 square feet.\n   - Octavia uses 6 large t-shirts.\n   - Total square footage from large t-shirts: \\( 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\) square feet.\n\n4. **Sum the square footage from all the t-shirts:**\n   - Total square footage: \\( 33 + 32 + 36 = 101 \\) square feet.\n\nThus, the total square footage of the quilt is \\(\\boxed{101}\\).", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "101", "gsm_numeric_answer": "101", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 283, "entry_transfer_id": "59c60a44-389d-45af-8c5f-4b08cd0c0e0e", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.10840312502114102, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
