{"id": "gsm8k:606", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790753984.7617118, "first_event_seconds": 0.9325355479959399, "wall_seconds": 73.42687898303848, "prompt_sha256": "e9bc80c6675001fb288e6d2e5e83f25924c8d1f973051447a5a9f71f2f1fef78", "prompt_tokens": 105, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 316, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "cd8a18ae170544d7a7990a9b4e842b1d", "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many years it will take for the tires to reach their maximum rotation limit.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of rotations per mile:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Rotations per mile} = \\frac{725 \\text{ rotations}}{2 \\text{ miles}} = 362.5 \\text{ rotations per mile}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of rotations per month:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Rotations per month} = 400 \\text{ miles} \\times 362.5 \\text{ rotations per mile} = 145,000 \\text{ rotations per month}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of rotations per year:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Rotations per year} = 145,000 \\text{ rotations per month} \\times 12 \\text{ months per year} = 1,740,000 \\text{ rotations per year}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the number of years before the tires need to be replaced:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Years before replacement} = \\frac{10,440,000 \\text{ rotations}}{1,740,000 \\text{ rotations per year}} = 6 \\text{ years}\n   \\]\n\n**Final answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "6", "gsm_numeric_answer": "6", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 316, "entry_transfer_id": "74888814-195e-4436-931c-b6cad84f83aa", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.10685145296156406, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
{"id": "gsm8k:442", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790754058.3027265, "first_event_seconds": 1.2714335329947062, "wall_seconds": 79.06075879296986, "prompt_sha256": "ec3b03b3aff6514031123455d97db12645c88c1a52dc1833bcb30b05f233c2f3", "prompt_tokens": 126, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 328, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "8bb32db553ab431eaac02c2547390d21", "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Initial Temperature:**\n   Marcus's house starts at 40 degrees.\n\n2. **Temperature Increase from Baking:**\n   Marcus spends 3 hours baking, and the oven raises the temperature by 5 degrees every hour.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Temperature increase} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\times 5 \\text{ degrees/hour} = 15 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n   Adding this to the initial temperature:\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ degrees} + 15 \\text{ degrees} = 55 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Temperature Decrease from Opening the Window:**\n   Marcus opens the window for 30 minutes, and the temperature drops by 2 degrees every 10 minutes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of 10-minute intervals in 30 minutes} = \\frac{30 \\text{ minutes}}{10 \\text{ minutes/interval}} = 3 \\text{ intervals}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Temperature decrease} = 3 \\text{ intervals} \\times 2 \\text{ degrees/interval} = 6 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n   Subtracting this from the temperature after baking:\n   \\[\n   55 \\text{ degrees} - 6 \\text{ degrees} = 49 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{49}\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "49", "gsm_numeric_answer": "49", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 328, "entry_transfer_id": "4495b77f-0595-42aa-b3f1-2de0b402a6a0", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.10596080200048164, "arm": "target", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
